      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried testing this change locally and found that with superproject enabled, a `repo sync -g G2` after `repo init -g G1` syncs only projects in both `G1` and `G2`, and projects in `G2` that aren\u0027t also in `G1` weren\u0027t synced. looks like it\u0027s caused from `_WriteManifestFile` generating a `superproject_override.xml` with only `G1` projects. is that behavior intentional?",
      "revId": "a97d7b1e2fef2f804cef273152da69cdc9bb50e8",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
